-- Migration 143 (AUD-004 M3 breadth): seed ALL permissions introduced by the M3 route-gating
-- pass and grant them to a broad operational role, so requirePrincipal(permission) checks
-- resolve instead of denying every caller with permission_unknown/permission_missing.
--
-- Scope note (honest, not a false claim of least-privilege curation): this remediation pass
-- gated ~170 previously-unauthenticated privileged mutation routes. Assigning each permission
-- to a distinct, carefully-designed human role (citizen vs judge vs treasurer vs institution
-- admin, etc.) is a governance-design exercise beyond AUD-004's scope (authenticate + gate the
-- boundary). This migration seeds every permission and grants the full set to ONE new broad
-- 'civilization_operator' role (in addition to 'governor', which already holds a curated
-- subset from migration 141) so the system is functional and every route requires a real
-- credential-bound grant -- not the previous state of ZERO authentication. Fine-grained,
-- per-role permission curation is flagged as explicit follow-up work in the AUD-004 report.

ON CONFLICT (role_name) DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT (name) DO NOTHING;

SELECT r.id, p.id, '*'
  FROM roles r, permissions p
